# OpenTrader Project Info (agent ops)

> Supersedes the 2026-07-31 "BEHAVIOR OVERRIDE" block, which instructed agents
> to `pkill llama-server` when the harness looked stuck. That instruction was
> wrong: llama-server is the harness's brain; killing it breaks gpu-sync and
> the whole loop. Never kill llama-server. Diagnose, then use systemd.

## Services (systemd --user — the single source of truth)

| Unit | Port | Role |
|------|------|------|
| `gpu-sync.service` | 5801 | Multi-GPU request router; backends: 5802 only |
| `opentrader-llama-gpu1.service` | 5802 | llama-server — DeepSeek-V4-Pro-Qwen3.5-9B-MTP (AMD RX 7900 GRE) |
| `opentrader-harness.service` | — | Trading harness (finnhub, stage 3, rule-primary) |
| `opentrader-dashboard.service` | 8097 | FastAPI dashboard |
| `opentrader-mcp-server.service` | 8092 | MCP server |

- 5803 (qwen2.5-7b) is RETIRED — do not reference or restart it.
- llama-swap :8080 is retired — harness talks to gpu-sync :5801 or llama :5802 directly.

## State files (written only by the harness via state/manager.py)

- `data/paper_state.json` — positions, cash, equity, fills, trade journal
- `data/high_level_state.json` — regime, strategy, posture
- `data/history/cycle_*.json` — per-cycle snapshots (dashboard PVA source)
- `/tmp/harness_watch.log` — harness stdout (tail -50 to inspect)

## Ops commands

```bash
# Check all units
systemctl --user status opentrader-harness.service opentrader-dashboard.service gpu-sync.service opentrader-llama-gpu1.service

# Restart the harness (safe — state persists on disk)
systemctl --user restart opentrader-harness.service

# Inspect
tail -50 /tmp/harness_watch.log
journalctl --user -u opentrader-harness.service -n 100 --no-pager
```

## Critical rules

- **Never `pkill` llama-server or harness.** Use `systemctl --user restart`.
- Never use `--reload` on dashboard.py (causes restart loops).
- Never modify `data/connections.json` or `risk/manager.py` RiskConfig values without a sandbox proof.
- Training needs VRAM — stop `opentrader-llama-gpu1.service` first, restart it after.
- If the harness looks stuck (regime HOLD, 0 positions, many cycles): check the VIX gate first
  (`data/vix_gate.py` — in calm markets the gate is *supposed* to be closed). A closed gate is
  not a crash. Report, don't kill.
- Sandbox-first: prove changes in `/home/mrc/opentrader-sandbox` before touching the live tree.

